{% set local_problem %}
<p>Rotten fascia boards are one of the most common problems we find on Arab homes — and one of the most overlooked. When gutters leak at seams, overflow due to clogs, or pull away from the house, water soaks into the fascia boards behind them. Over time, this moisture leads to rot.</p>

<p>Arab's elevation doesn't protect against this. Alabama's humidity reaches into the mountains, and the temperature swings common at higher elevations can actually accelerate wood decay. Morning fog adds moisture that valley homes don't see as often. Those constant wet-dry cycles stress wood fibers and feed the fungi that cause rot.</p>

<p>The problem compounds over time. Rotten wood absorbs more water, accelerating decay. It attracts wood-destroying insects like carpenter ants and termites. Eventually, the damage spreads to rafters, sheathing, and even interior walls. What starts as a simple fascia board replacement becomes a major structural repair.</p>

<p><strong>If you're replacing gutters and the existing ones have been leaking for years:</strong> Expect some fascia damage. About 40% of gutter replacement jobs on older Arab homes involve some fascia repair. It's not a surprise expense — it's a predictable one. Better to budget for it upfront than discover soft wood on installation day.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our wood repair process ensures your new gutters have a solid foundation:</p>

<p><strong>Inspection:</strong> We carefully examine all fascia boards, soffit panels, and trim. We probe suspicious areas with a screwdriver to determine the extent of damage — paint can hide a lot. Visual inspection alone misses hidden rot. If it looks suspicious, we press on it.</p>

<p><strong>Assessment:</strong> We document what needs repair and explain our findings. You'll understand exactly what's damaged, why it matters, and what we recommend to fix it. No scare tactics — just honest information.</p>

<p><strong>Removal:</strong> We remove old gutters and damaged wood, taking care not to spread rot to healthy areas. Debris is disposed of properly.</p>

<p><strong>Repair:</strong> We install new fascia boards, soffit panels, or trim as needed. Standard pine fascia runs $5-10/linear foot and lasts 10-12 years with proper paint maintenance. Composite or PVC fascia runs $12-20/linear foot but lasts 20+ years with virtually no maintenance. We prime all cuts to prevent future moisture intrusion.</p>

<p><strong>Preparation:</strong> With solid wood in place, we install your new gutters properly — anchored securely with hardware that will hold for decades.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've repaired rotten wood on many <a href="/recent-projects/">Arab homes</a> and understand how damage patterns develop in this climate. We're not just gutter installers — we're craftsmen who understand the carpentry required to do the job right.</p>

<p>We won't pressure you into unnecessary repairs, and we won't install new gutters on failing wood. Our goal is a gutter system that protects your home for decades — and that requires starting with a solid foundation.</p>

<p><strong>Warning from experience:</strong> If someone says your fascia "looks fine" without actually pressing on it, get a second opinion. We've seen plenty of paint hiding soft, spongy wood underneath. Visual inspection isn't enough — you have to test it.</p>

